1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,837
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:08,466
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,719
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,349
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:19,185
[in English] Are you sure
we are in the right place?

7
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:21,980
[security officer, in English] <i>Our intel</i>
<i>told us that the decoder of this town</i>

8
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,565
<i>is the mayor's niece.</i>

9
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:26,901
[Samir, in English] <i>The man who broke</i>
<i>into the ambassador's office.</i>

10
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:28,278
[in English] He might be here too.

11
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:30,321
[in English] <i>Take a good look at him.</i>

12
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,407
[Cita] <i>You shouldn't be</i>
<i>coming here anymore.</i>

13
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,617
Didn't Atoy forbid you?

14
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,702
I'll go ahead.

15
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:37,537
Well, the watch was exposed
as fake right away.

16
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,663
I hadn't even left yet.

17
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:40,999
The money was inside the bag. I left it.

18
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:44,210
[Emerson] <i>You're the woman earlier</i>
<i>at the mall parking lot.</i>

19
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:45,920
[Ame] <i>What are you saying?</i>
<i>Maybe she just looks like the woman.</i>

20
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:48,590
- She is Ibyang's mother!
- Huh?

21
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:51,217
[Audrey] <i>Do you know the man</i>
<i>who tried to take my child?</i>

22
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:52,510
[Red] <i>Why would I know him?</i>

23
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:54,262
<i>I'm not a child trafficker.</i>

24
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:55,555
[Audrey] <i>Are you sure?</i>

25
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:57,599
[Ibyang] <i>You're a liar!</i>

26
00:00:57,682 --> 00:00:59,142
<i>It's impossible you're my mother.</i>

27
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:00,310
You're a scammer!

28
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:02,937
What do you want me to do
so you'll believe me, Ibyang?

29
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:06,483
- I used to be a scammer too.
- Hmm?

30
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:09,986
[in Visayan] I was hoping to invite you
to watch a performance outside.

31
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:12,280
[in Visayan] I'm scared
someone might see me.

32
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:15,617
[in Visayan] <i>I know you're afraid</i>
<i>of being seen by the ambassador.</i>

33
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,995
[in Visayan] <i>But let me tell you,</i>
<i>you're safe here.</i>

34
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:21,873
[Lily, in Visayan]
<i>I know, but can I stay here?</i>

35
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:24,125
<i>I feel safer here.</i>

36
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:26,795
[dagger swishes]

37
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:34,552
[tense music playing]

38
00:01:38,807 --> 00:01:39,724
[music fades]

39
00:01:40,517 --> 00:01:42,393
[suspicious music playing]

40
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:46,981
[in Visayan] Our guest will be happy
when they watch you.

41
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:48,691
[woman, in Visayan]
You can see it clearly.

42
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:52,028
[in Visayan] Do better
on your performance at the fiesta.

43
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,404
[in Visayna] You can count on us, ma'am.

44
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:55,824
- Thank you.
- [in Visayan] Thank you, Mayor.

45
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:59,452
[ominous music playing]

46
00:02:15,593 --> 00:02:17,095
[secretary, in English] Oh.
Picture, Mayor.

47
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:18,096
[chuckles softly]

48
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:23,560
[man] Stop!

49
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:27,772
- [screaming and panicking]
- [foreboding music playing]

50
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:29,649
Son of a thread.

51
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,818
[guard] Cover the Mayor!

52
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:33,611
Cover him! Cover the Mayor!

53
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:34,612
We're escaping!

54
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,739
[clamoring]

55
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:46,833
[Mercado on the device] <i>Lily Santiago,</i>
<i>the head of IT of the embassy.</i>

56
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:47,959
[tense music playing]

57
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:50,420
- Come.
- God-- Let go of me.

58
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:52,839
- Godfather, help! Godfather, he…
- [hushes]

59
00:02:52,922 --> 00:02:55,008
- Shut! Shut up.
- [whimpering]

60
00:02:55,091 --> 00:02:56,384
[mutters]

61
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:58,636
I won't hurt you.

62
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:00,722
Why should I believe you?

63
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:02,682
Because I'm not the one firing shots.

64
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:05,184
The embassy people are there.
They want to take you.

65
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:06,561
- Come.
- [gasps]

66
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:10,940
- Come.
- [gasps]

67
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,525
[guard] Cover the Mayor!

68
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:13,693
We're escaping!

69
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:14,819
Hurry!

70
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:23,786
[music swells]

71
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,374
[music fades]

72
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:32,629
[rousing music playing]

73
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:33,671
[in English] Go.

74
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:38,676
[in English] Good evening, Mr. Mayor.

75
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:45,350
[in English] Where is she?

76
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:49,646
- [music swells]
- [soft sobs]

77
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:01,366
[music fades]

78
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:02,700
[armed man] Where are you going?!

79
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:04,577
[suave theme music playing]

80
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:07,372
[motorcycle revving]

81
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:09,290
[sewing machine whirring]

82
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,250
[scratches]

83
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:11,834
[snipping]

84
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:15,171
[sewing machine clacking]

85
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:16,422
[gun cocks]

86
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:18,549
[gunshots]

87
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:20,843
[gunshots]

88
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:22,262
[clicking]

89
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:23,388
[snipping]

90
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:27,308
[electronic blipping]

91
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:31,479
[music fades]

92
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:32,605
[woman sobs softly]

93
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:34,899
[in English] I don't want to play games.

94
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:36,859
[groans]

95
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,237
[in English] I will ask you one more time.

96
00:04:40,571 --> 00:04:42,240
[in English] Where is she?

97
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:44,450
- [music fades]
- [woman sobs softly]

98
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:46,452
- [grunts and groans]
- [thumps]

99
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,663
- [gunshot]
- [grunting]

100
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:50,957
[groans]

101
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,543
[grunting]

102
00:04:53,626 --> 00:04:55,211
[groans]

103
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:59,674
[action music playing]

104
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:01,968
[music fades]

105
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:06,347
[action music playing]

106
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:18,151
[tense music playing]

107
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:22,697
[sobs]

108
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:24,824
[in English] Maybe I'll ask your wife.

109
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:27,785
[in English] Maybe she's smarter than you.

110
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:29,078
[sobs]

111
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:31,622
[suspicious music playing]

112
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:33,499
- [in English] Where is the girl?
- [sobs]

113
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:37,378
[in Visayan] Don't say anything!
Don't say anything!

114
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:41,883
[wailing]

115
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:43,843
[in English] Where is she?!

116
00:05:43,926 --> 00:05:46,554
[wails, in English] Last room on the left.

117
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:51,017
[in English] Please, let go
of my husband! [wails]

118
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,644
[in English] Thank you very much.
Thank you very much.

119
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:56,189
[wails]

120
00:05:56,272 --> 00:05:57,273
[Samir, in English] Let's go.

121
00:05:58,107 --> 00:06:00,401
[tense music playing]

122
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:04,238
[wails]

123
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:05,990
[music fades]

124
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:07,116
[in English] This is bad.

125
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:09,494
Dad needs to know about this.

126
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:18,086
[pensive music playing]

127
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:20,588
[Red] Mongki, we'll need
to expand eventually.

128
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:24,050
[muffled chattering in the distance]

129
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:28,471
[tense music playing]

130
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,640
Yes, but…

131
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:32,809
maybe you should get more people.

132
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:35,520
[Mongki] Okay, boss. I'll handle it.

133
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:36,729
I already have someone to talk to.

134
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:41,859
[Red] The people you recruit need to be
better than the ones you've hired before.

135
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,361
[Mongki, in English] Yes, boss.

136
00:06:44,862 --> 00:06:47,365
[Red] This new shipment is big.

137
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,325
So, you need

138
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,036
to talk to the client first.

139
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:55,832
So, maybe you should go see him.

140
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,792
[both speaking indistinctly]

141
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:03,422
[tense music playing]

142
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:04,507
[squeals]

143
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:11,055
[door lock clicks]

144
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:40,501
[in English] Bring the Mayor back to me.

145
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:42,295
[music fades]

146
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,631
I already sent the files to the client.

147
00:07:47,216 --> 00:07:49,635
I'll tell the boys, boss,
so they'll be ready.

148
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,637
[mysterious music playing]

149
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:52,555
Do you smell that?

150
00:07:54,765 --> 00:07:56,058
It smells like perfume for women.

151
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,226
- But it's not Martina's.
- [sniffling]

152
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:00,271
Oh, I don't smell anything, boss.

153
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:02,190
[Mongki sniffs]

154
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:07,028
[music swells]

155
00:08:10,656 --> 00:08:11,574
[smirks]

156
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,284
[ominous music playing]

157
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:15,912
Sir, they're here, sir!

158
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:17,872
[armed man on the device]
<i>We're about to catch them, sir!</i>

159
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:22,627
[in English] Let's go.

160
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:29,634
[music swells]

161
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:32,803
Hmm.

162
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:35,932
You're disgusting too, aren't you?

163
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:37,058
Hold your glass.

164
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:39,685
I'm drunk. I don't remember this.

165
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:42,396
[suspicious music playing]

166
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:53,199
[sniffs]

167
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:57,411
[music swells]

168
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:01,457
[music fades]

169
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:02,667
[groans]

170
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,210
[grunting]

171
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:06,462
[groaning and grunting]

172
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:16,180
[upbeat rock music playing]

173
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:17,139
Let's go.

174
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:39,870
[music fades]

175
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:45,626
- [ominous music playing]
- [groans]

176
00:09:58,889 --> 00:10:01,267
[groans]

177
00:10:09,191 --> 00:10:13,738
[suspicious music playing]

178
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:17,950
[in English] This is a… new costume.

179
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:20,786
[panting]

180
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:21,996
[in English] Do you like it?

181
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:29,879
[in English] Before I do something to you,

182
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:34,717
I want to see your face.

183
00:10:35,968 --> 00:10:38,346
[groans]

184
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:48,773
[in English] Take them.

185
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,983
[music swells]

186
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,068
[dramatic sting]

187
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,866
[music fades]

188
00:11:01,952 --> 00:11:03,371
[Martina, in English]
What are you doing here?

189
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:04,997
[ominous music playing]

190
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:08,042
You. Aren't you going home yet?

191
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:12,880
Well, I smelled something strange.

192
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:15,758
- [suspicious music playing]
- [sniffs]

193
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:17,927
The only strange smell is you.

194
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,553
[in English] You reek of alcohol.

195
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,765
[in English] Obviously I'm drunk, right?

196
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:24,642
Let's go.

197
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,238
So?

198
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:39,156
- Did you see anything?
- [inhales]

199
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:42,118
Hey. We might trend later
as scammers, huh!

200
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:44,662
Well, there's nothing!

201
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:46,122
Nothing at all.

202
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:52,002
Maybe they didn't report it
because their money was returned, right?

203
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:56,132
Friend, maybe you should focus
on Ibyang first.

204
00:11:57,049 --> 00:11:58,884
- Make peace with her.
- [gentle music playing]

205
00:11:58,968 --> 00:12:01,679
Oh? I'm okay now.

206
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,306
I just don't…

207
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:06,016
I just don't want to get attached

208
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:08,269
because it hurts when you lose someone.

209
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:10,521
Sammy is different.

210
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,773
Maybe you're right.

211
00:12:13,607 --> 00:12:17,403
The child isn't doing anything wrong
for me to treat her that way.

212
00:12:17,486 --> 00:12:19,113
[gentle music playing]

213
00:12:19,196 --> 00:12:21,282
There. Thank you, Lord.

214
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:24,618
You softened my friend's heart of stone.

215
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:26,036
So, what?

216
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:29,206
What are you thinking of doing
so you two can set things right?

217
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:31,167
I want to be with you.

218
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:35,337
On Christmas, on my birthday.

219
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:38,883
So many occasions have already passed.

220
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:46,015
I have an idea.

221
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:47,558
What?

222
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:53,772
[sentimental music playing]

223
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:57,818
[in English] Dad? [gasps]

224
00:12:57,902 --> 00:12:59,445
Dad, are you still awake?

225
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:04,783
[suspicious music playing]

226
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:05,993
[in English] No choice.

227
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:08,829
This has to stop, Red.

228
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:10,623
[sighs]

229
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:12,917
Which one, Ma?

230
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:16,712
Ah, the plastic one there with a cover
and the handle.

231
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:18,172
[softly] This one.

232
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:20,090
Ah…

233
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:23,010
This one?

234
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:24,803
[in English] Thank you, baby girl!

235
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:26,805
Oh, later, I have a surprise for you.

236
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:43,322
[gentle music playing]

237
00:13:57,211 --> 00:14:00,089
This must be Mama's surprise.

238
00:14:00,881 --> 00:14:02,049
[gasps in awe]

239
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:06,512
[music fades]

240
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:11,433
[in English] Boss, what are we
going to do with them?

241
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:15,646
[in English] We have to find out
who he works for.

242
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:19,984
[in English] We have to get back
what they took from us.

243
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:20,943
[in English] Okay.

244
00:14:21,443 --> 00:14:23,946
[in English] But what if he doesn't talk?

245
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:32,329
[in English] Then we will squeeze
this information from them.

246
00:14:41,046 --> 00:14:42,423
[music fades]

247
00:14:44,008 --> 00:14:44,884
Audrey.

248
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:47,469
Where are you taking that?

249
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:51,932
[pensive music playing]

250
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:54,977
I don't know how
you can stomach doing this.

251
00:14:55,895 --> 00:15:01,442
Even my own child almost became a victim
because of what you've been doing!

252
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:03,235
[in English] This has to stop!

253
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:04,695
[in English] You're a monster!

254
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:07,573
[in English] You don't know
what you're talking about.

255
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:08,532
Give me that.

256
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:10,576
[in English] I don't know
what I'm talking about?

257
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:12,828
[in English] You're really
out of your mind!

258
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:13,787
[in English] You know that?

259
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:15,998
I've known this for a long time.

260
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,459
So, give it to me. Come on.

261
00:15:18,542 --> 00:15:19,460
[in English] No!

262
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,962
Dad has to see this.

263
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:24,173
[in English] Dad?

264
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:26,592
You'll complain to him?

265
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:28,052
[tense music playing]

266
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:29,637
[in English] He knows this!

267
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:32,014
No one will defend you.

268
00:15:32,848 --> 00:15:36,310
[music swells]

269
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,982
[music fades]

270
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,735
[in English] Ibyang, baby girl!

271
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:46,278
[mellow music playing]

272
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:50,908
[in English] Happy birthdays
and Merry Christmases to you, my child.

273
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:55,537
Didn't you say
so many occasions have passed?

274
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:56,747
But don't worry.

275
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:58,749
We'll catch up on all of them, okay?

276
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:00,584
Oh, go ahead. Make a wish.

277
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,257
[Olga chuckles]

278
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:09,259
[in English] Thank you, Mama.

279
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:12,012
Thank you also for

280
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:12,930
your gift.

281
00:16:13,013 --> 00:16:14,223
I already got it.

282
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:16,684
What gift?

283
00:16:20,729 --> 00:16:21,897
[Ibyang] This one.

284
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:27,236
This is the first time
I've had such a beautiful doll.

285
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:35,661
You're a meddler!

286
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:39,415
Did I tell you to take this?!

287
00:16:40,290 --> 00:16:42,793
Did I tell you to touch this?!

288
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:44,003
Did I?!

289
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:45,045
[heavy breathing]

290
00:16:45,129 --> 00:16:50,926
Didn't I tell you not to touch
any of my things here unless I say so?!

291
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,053
This is your fault, huh!

292
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:55,139
It's your fault this got broken!

293
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:57,307
You're a meddler!

294
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:04,148
[music fades]

295
00:17:05,482 --> 00:17:08,736
[melodramatic music playing]

296
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:32,009
[Olga sobs, in English] Sorry.

297
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:34,011
[in English] So-Sorry, Sammy.
Sorry, sorry.

298
00:17:36,430 --> 00:17:40,225
[sobbing]

299
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:52,696
[electronic blipping]

300
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:57,451
Sammy!

301
00:17:57,534 --> 00:17:59,828
Child, come on. Let's have snacks!

302
00:17:59,912 --> 00:18:03,791
Mommy, can I eat here in the room instead?

303
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:05,709
Huh?

304
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:07,211
No, you can't!

305
00:18:07,294 --> 00:18:09,671
[in English] Mommy, please?

306
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:12,174
Sammy.

307
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:14,635
[in English] I said no.

308
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:16,678
Come down here. Come on.

309
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:19,306
[thuds]

310
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:20,265
Hey.

311
00:18:20,849 --> 00:18:22,976
Are you stomping your feet?!

312
00:18:23,852 --> 00:18:25,938
Don't be like that. I'll get angry.

313
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:31,110
[thudding]

314
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:33,695
Sammy!

315
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:35,239
Sam! [panicked breathing]

316
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:37,574
Sam, Sam, my child! Sam.
[panicked breathing]

317
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,660
Sammy! Sammy!

318
00:18:39,743 --> 00:18:41,745
[unsettling music playing]

319
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,831
Sam, Sam!

320
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:48,919
[sobbing]

321
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:53,549
[music fades]

322
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:56,718
[melancholic music playing]

323
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:07,688
[door lock clicks]

324
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,197
[sighs]

325
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:20,951
Olga, the vehicle is here.

326
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:24,079
Let's go?

327
00:19:26,039 --> 00:19:27,875
Um… [inhales]

328
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:32,713
They'll bring Sammy's remains
to the funeral house already.

329
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:34,339
We need to be there first.

330
00:19:44,099 --> 00:19:46,018
I can't. [sobs]

331
00:19:49,563 --> 00:19:52,816
I can't, Charm… Charmi.

332
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,359
I can't…

333
00:19:59,823 --> 00:20:01,241
I can't--

334
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:08,540
[sobbing]

335
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:11,793
What they're saying is true. [sniffles]

336
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:15,964
I'm a bad mother.

337
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:18,342
[music fades]

338
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:21,470
I neglected my child.

339
00:20:22,262 --> 00:20:24,056
[sobbing]

340
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:26,141
She's gone.

341
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:28,060
She's gone.

342
00:20:28,143 --> 00:20:30,979
[sobbing]

343
00:20:31,063 --> 00:20:36,276
[melodramatic music playing]

344
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,569
Hey.

345
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:38,862
[sobs]

346
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:40,072
What are you saying?

347
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:41,573
That's not true.

348
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:44,117
It was an accident.

349
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:48,330
Don't believe what they're saying,

350
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:49,706
that you're a bad mother.

351
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:51,541
They don't know anything.

352
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:53,669
It was an accident,

353
00:20:54,461 --> 00:20:56,505
and you didn't want that.

354
00:20:56,588 --> 00:20:58,966
You loved your child so much.

355
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:00,092
Hmm?

356
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:05,555
[sobbing]

357
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:21,238
[music fades]

358
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:28,328
[in English] I'm sorry, Sammy.

359
00:21:29,705 --> 00:21:31,623
[in English] Sorry.

360
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:32,916
[in English] Sorry.

361
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:38,255
[melancholic music playing]

362
00:21:39,172 --> 00:21:44,970
[sobbing]

363
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:53,353
[in English] Sorry, Mama.

364
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:58,984
[sobbing]

365
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,533
Don't call me Mama.

366
00:22:07,826 --> 00:22:09,077
You're not my child!

367
00:22:09,953 --> 00:22:11,371
[music fades]

368
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:16,668
[dramatic music playing]

369
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:44,279
[music fades]

370
00:22:44,362 --> 00:22:45,322
[in English] No.

371
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:47,491
No. No. I don't believe you.

372
00:22:48,366 --> 00:22:49,785
Dad has changed.

373
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:52,079
[sniffs, in English] Okay.

374
00:22:52,579 --> 00:22:53,997
[in English] Check it. [sniffs]

375
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:56,166
[in English] Now!

376
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:01,463
There.

377
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:11,515
[Red, in English] I'm sure
you know that seal, right?

378
00:23:13,183 --> 00:23:14,601
[in English] It's his personal seal.

379
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:16,311
He knows this.

380
00:23:16,895 --> 00:23:17,896
[in English] He is the mastermind!

381
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:19,147
[suspicious music playing]

382
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:20,315
[Dmitri, in English] <i>Where's my ring?</i>

383
00:23:20,398 --> 00:23:22,150
Looks like it's not here.

384
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:24,611
[in English] Oh. Found it.

385
00:23:25,403 --> 00:23:26,321
[Dmitri] Oh.

386
00:23:28,365 --> 00:23:30,117
[Red] So, it's useless
if you complain to him.

387
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:33,078
Unless you want our family's dirt
to be made public.

388
00:23:34,496 --> 00:23:35,580
Is that what you want?

389
00:23:37,999 --> 00:23:39,167
[Dmitri clears throat]

390
00:23:46,466 --> 00:23:47,968
[in English] What's with the look?

391
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:49,136
[in English] What's going on here?

392
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:50,137
[in English] Dad…

393
00:23:52,472 --> 00:23:54,057
Are you involved in this?

394
00:23:58,895 --> 00:24:00,272
- You know--
- [Dmitri] Red.

395
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:02,649
[in English] Leave us.

396
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:05,152
[music fades]

397
00:24:07,946 --> 00:24:11,908
[somber music playing]

398
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:13,368
[in English] Answer me!

399
00:24:13,451 --> 00:24:16,955
[tense music playing]

400
00:24:17,038 --> 00:24:21,793
[in English] Are you involved
in human trafficking?

401
00:24:23,587 --> 00:24:25,338
[in English] Audrey, let me explain.

402
00:24:25,422 --> 00:24:26,631
- [in English] No.
- Audrey.

403
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:27,549
[thuds]

404
00:24:31,386 --> 00:24:32,846
[in English] I trusted you!

405
00:24:33,638 --> 00:24:36,141
[sobs] I chose you over Atoy!

406
00:24:36,224 --> 00:24:38,351
I chose this family!

407
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:41,146
But you were deceiving me!

408
00:24:43,273 --> 00:24:45,901
There's really no one decent
in this family!

409
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:52,032
Don't touch me!

410
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:56,077
[music swells]

411
00:25:00,540 --> 00:25:06,713
[tense music playing]

412
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:16,848
[gasping]

413
00:25:17,515 --> 00:25:18,516
Brother!

414
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:20,894
[Lily] Ouch.

415
00:25:20,977 --> 00:25:23,438
Brother! Brother, wake up, brother!

416
00:25:23,521 --> 00:25:25,815
[gasping]

417
00:25:25,899 --> 00:25:27,234
Where are we?

418
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:29,402
How will we escape from here? Brother!

419
00:25:29,486 --> 00:25:30,946
[gasping]

420
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:32,030
Brother!

421
00:25:32,113 --> 00:25:34,199
[panting]

422
00:25:34,282 --> 00:25:35,158
Ouch.

423
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:36,952
[music swells]

424
00:25:37,035 --> 00:25:38,036
[Lily] Ouch.

425
00:25:39,663 --> 00:25:41,498
Bro-- Brother!

426
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:43,083
Psst, hey!

427
00:25:43,166 --> 00:25:44,793
Brother! [sobs]

428
00:25:44,876 --> 00:25:46,920
[music swells]

429
00:25:47,003 --> 00:25:49,422
[tense music playing]

430
00:25:49,506 --> 00:25:52,008
[electronic blipping]

431
00:25:58,223 --> 00:25:59,599
Where are we going?

432
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:00,725
To the States.

433
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:03,520
[Audrey] <i>But, we need to go</i>
<i>to your Daddy Atoy first.</i>

434
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:04,479
UP NEXT

435
00:26:04,562 --> 00:26:05,522
[Janine] Mommy.

436
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:07,107
No one leaves.

437
00:26:09,276 --> 00:26:10,610
[henchman 1] I'm sure, boss. It's here.

438
00:26:12,028 --> 00:26:13,238
[people screaming]

439
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:14,990
[gasps and squeals]

440
00:26:15,073 --> 00:26:16,616
[screaming and panicking]

441
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:18,785
- [grunts]
- [in English] No, no, no, no, no!

442
00:26:18,868 --> 00:26:19,869
- [grunts and groans]
- [Lily, in English] No!

443
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:22,122
- [Lily sobs]
- [Atoy coughs]

444
00:26:22,205 --> 00:26:24,457
[in English] I need you
to report to me in person.

445
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,751
[in English] Padua is compromised.

446
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:30,380
[Samir, in English] If you do not want
to make this simple,

447
00:26:31,172 --> 00:26:34,759
I will make it very, very hard for you.

448
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:36,177
[in English] No!

449
00:26:36,261 --> 00:26:38,763
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

450
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:41,599
- [in English] No, please!
- [Samir grunts]

451
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:42,434
[grunts]

452
00:26:42,517 --> 00:26:45,395
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

453
00:26:45,478 --> 00:26:47,439
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

454
00:26:47,522 --> 00:26:49,941
‪Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
